# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PAER-LLM
#
# Rule of thumb: if a file can be regenerated by running the pipeline,
# it does not belong in git. The corpus, the derived feature tables and
# the trained weights are all regenerable; the code, the configuration,
# the fold assignments and the per-fold predictions are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- environments ---
venv/
.venv/
env/
.conda/

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

# --- corpus -----------------------------------------------------------
# RAVDESS is ~1 GB and is distributed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 from Zenodo.
# It is not redistributed here; see the README for where to put it.
Dataset/

# --- derived features -------------------------------------------------
# hubert_embeddings.csv is ~26 MB and multimodal_features.csv ~45 MB.
# Both are deterministic functions of Dataset/ and the extraction code,
# so committing them would add ~70 MB to every clone for no reproducibility
# benefit. Regenerate with the Features/ scripts.
Outputs/*.csv
Outputs/*.npy

# --- trained weights --------------------------------------------------
# Force-add a specific checkpoint if you ever need to ship one:
#   git add -f Models/best_model.pth
Models/*.pth
Models/*.pkl
Models/*.npy

# --- archives ---------------------------------------------------------
# Including the paper's Overleaf bundle: the .tex sources next to it are
# the tracked copy, and a zip of them would drift out of sync silently.
*.zip

# --- LaTeX build artefacts -------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.lof
*.lot
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.spl
Paper/**/*.log

# --- scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
_backup_original/
_superseded/
_to_delete/
Streamlit/temp.wav
requirement.txt.txt

# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
